<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 59,836 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 59,836 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 59,836 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 72,345 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 8,805	   11,255</p>
<p>    Import cargo			51,031	   61,090</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, two ships were expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:Z Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>High speed diesel    73,000	 Chesapeak City     1/2</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,090	 Johar		 26/1</p>
<p>Jet feul		 25,000	 Ras Al-Zour	  3/2</p>
<p>Palm oil		 15,000	 Wawasan Megah     29/1</p>
<p>High speed diesel    27,300	 Chilham Castle    23/1</p>
<p>Chemicals		10,550	 Bakri Orbitor     30/1</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Courage    5/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
